# AnkiKOAi — local dev context (Cursor / AI)

Copy this file to **`LOCAL_DEV.md`** (gitignored) and edit machine-specific paths:

```bash
cp LOCAL_DEV.md.sample LOCAL_DEV.md
```

**Cursor:** attach `@LOCAL_DEV.md` at session start, or rely on `.cursor/rules/ankikooai-dev.mdc`
**Cursor (v3+ / Glass):** `.code-workspace` files require the **Editor** window first — **Ctrl+Shift+N**
(or **File → Open Editor Window**), then **Ctrl+Shift+P** → **Open Workspace from File...** →
`C:\Users\small\koreader-dev.code-workspace`. CLI: `cursor C:\Users\small\koreader-dev.code-workspace --classic`.
Both plugin repos live in **`C:\Users\small\`**.

---

## Ecosystem (3-folder workspace)

| Folder | Role |
|--------|------|
| **AnkiKOAi.koplugin** (this repo) | Highlights → Wiki / Vocab / Mem cards → AnkiConnect → desktop Anki |
| **tagbankhighlightsync.koplugin** | Tag bank, JSON sync via cloud, Markdown quote library (`C:\Users\small\`) |
| **KOReader Highlights** (Desktop) | PC WebDAV root (`webdav.exe` :8181) + Obsidian vault for generated `library/` |

**Workflow:** Read on KOReader → AnkiKOAi sends cards to Anki; TagBankHighlightSync tags highlights,
syncs `*.sdr.json`, and exports quote Markdown into `KOReader Highlights/library/`. JSON on WebDAV
is the source of truth; Markdown is derived on **Sync now**.

**Dev hub:** `bash dev-start.sh --emulator alice.epub` from **this repo** syncs both plugins and
launches once. TagBank’s `dev-start.sh` delegates here.

**Two cloud concepts (do not conflate):**

- **Tools → Cloud storage** — WebDAV account list (`settings/cloudstorage.lua`)
- **Tag Bank Highlight Sync → Cloud folder** — sync target path (`sync_server` in plugin settings)

Emulator one-time (TagBank repo): `setup-emulator-cloud.sh` + `configure-emulator-webdav.sh`.

**AI read order:** (1) this file’s **Your goals & current focus**, (2) repo-specific sections below,
(3) sibling `LOCAL_DEV.md.sample` only when the task crosses repos (sync, quote library, dev-start).

