## Starting KOReader (development)

From repo root in **WSL**:

```bash
# Recommended: sync AnkiKOAi + TagBankHighlightSync, launch once (avoids second-launch COPY MODE)
bash dev-start.sh --emulator alice.epub

# One-time: Cloud storage+ for TagBankHighlightSync (from tagbankhighlightsync repo):
# bash /mnt/c/Users/small/tagbankhighlightsync.koplugin/setup-emulator-cloud.sh
# bash /mnt/c/Users/small/tagbankhighlightsync.koplugin/configure-emulator-webdav.sh

# Sync both without opening KOReader:
bash dev-start.sh --sync-only

# This plugin only:
bash start.sh --sync-only
bash start.sh --emulator alice.epub

# With log capture (recommended when debugging):
bash dev-start.sh --emulator alice.epub 2>&1 | tee ~/koreader-emulator.log
```

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
|----------|---------|---------|
| `KOREADER_DIR` | `~/koreader-dev/emulator/usr/lib/koreader` | Emulator tree |
| `ANKIKOOAI_SRC` | This repo | AnkiKOAi rsync source |
| `TAGBANKHIGHLIGHTSYNC_SRC` | `/mnt/c/Users/small/tagbankhighlightsync.koplugin` | TagBankHighlightSync rsync source |
| `PLUGIN_DST` | `~/koreader-dev/plugins/AnkiKOAi.koplugin` | AnkiKOAi rsync target |

**WSL default** (`bash start.sh` without flags) is **AppImage mode** — does **not** sync plugins.
AppImage from WSL still uses **WSLg**; `[WARN: COPY MODE]` may appear in the **taskbar** only.

**Avoid two full `./luajit reader.lua` launches in one WSL session** — the second often triggers
WSLg COPY MODE. Use `dev-start.sh` or `start.sh --sync-only` + one launch.

**Machine-specific (edit in your `LOCAL_DEV.md`):**

- WSL distro: `<!-- e.g. Ubuntu -->`
- Repo path: `<!-- e.g. /mnt/c/Users/you/AnkiKOAi.koplugin -->`
- Emulator data: `<!-- ~/koreader-dev/emulator/usr/lib/koreader/ -->`

### KOReader Highlights (WebDAV + quote library)

PC folder: `C:\Users\small\Desktop\KOReader Highlights` (WebDAV root, port 8181).
Setup: `KOReader-WebDAV-Setup.md` in that folder. Generated on sync: `alice.sdr.json`,
`library/books/*.md`, `library/master-quotes.md`, `library/tags/*.md`.

Regenerate library from JSON without emulator (from TagBank repo):

```bash
~/koreader-dev/emulator/usr/lib/koreader/luajit \
  /mnt/c/Users/small/tagbankhighlightsync.koplugin/spec/validate_webdav_library.lua \
  "/mnt/c/Users/small/Desktop/KOReader Highlights/alice.sdr.json" \
  "/mnt/c/Users/small/Desktop/KOReader Highlights/library"
```

Quote-library validation steps: TagBank `LOCAL_DEV.md.sample` § Quote library validation.

