## Logging

KOReader dev emulator logs to **stdout** (terminal), not always to a file.

| Log | Typical path |
|-----|----------------|
| Captured session | `~/koreader-emulator.log` (via `tee` above) |
| Emulator data dir | `~/koreader-dev/emulator/usr/lib/koreader/` (`ankikooai_*.json`, `settings/`) |

**Useful grep after a crash:**

```bash
grep -E 'stack traceback|ERROR |WARN |ankikooai|AnkiKOAi|init failed' ~/koreader-emulator.log
```

Plugin uses KOReader `logger` (`require("logger")`) → stdout. `main.lua` wraps highlight
`init()` in `pcall`; failures show `ankikooai init failed:`.

**Highlight dialog rule:** `addToHighlightDialog` callbacks must **never return `nil`**.
Use `show_in_highlight_dialog_func = function() return false end` to hide a button.
Hub button id: `99_ankikooai` (`PluginConstants.HIGHLIGHT_DIALOG_ID_HUB`) — KOReader sorts
buttons by id string; `97_` / `98_` / `99_` prefixes keep plugin entries after core
highlight actions (scroll if many plugins). **View All Highlights** = `97_ankikooai_view_all`.

**View All Highlights** opens `highlight_inbox.lua` — highlights for the current book (or **Switch book** for any book in reading history with sidecar highlights). **Sync All Highlights** runs Tag Bank cloud sync for every book in history (when Tag Bank is installed). Delete works only for the open book; batch Anki send works from sidecar text on other books.
Also: **AnkiKOAi hub → View All Highlights** or **Highlights and Cards → Highlights to Anki**.

**Dev-only reset script:** `scripts/reset_alice.sh` — PC Alice clean-slate (Anki, WebDAV, Obsidian); requires TagBank regen script in sibling repo.

